    "q-14951": {
      "dom_id": "step-q14951",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Calculate $L={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\sqrt[n]{{a}_{n}}$ for the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{5}^{n}{n}^{n+1}}{(9+5n)^{n}}.$ According to the root test, does ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ converge or diverge?",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose we have the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ such that ${a}_{n}\\ge 0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and that $L$ is defined as  \n\n$$\nL={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\sqrt[n]{{a}_{n}}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{({a}_{n})}^{1/n}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, the root test states the following:\n\n- If $L<1$, the series converges.\n\n- If $L>1$ or $L=\\infty $, the series diverges.\n\n- If $L=1$, the root test is inconclusive.\n\nWe have the sequence ${a}_{n},$ defined as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{{5}^{n}{n}^{n+1}}{(9+5n)^{n}}.\n$$\n\nTo apply the root test, we find the limit of $\\sqrt[n]{{a}_{n}}$ as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\sqrt[n]{{a}_{n}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{({a}_{n})}^{1/n} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{{5}^{n}{n}^{n+1}}{(9+5n)^{n}})}^{1/n} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{{5}^{n}{n}^{n}\\cdot n}{(9+5n)^{n}})}^{1/n} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{5n\\sqrt[n]{n}}{9+5n} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\sqrt[n]{n}\\cdot \\frac{5n}{n})}{(\\frac{9}{n}+\\frac{5n}{n})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{5\\sqrt[n]{n}}{(\\frac{9}{n}+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 1}{0+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\sqrt[n]{n}=1.\n$$\n\nSince $L=1,$ the root test gives no conclusion.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-14951-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$L=\\frac{1}{9}.$ The series is convergent.",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"51\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D43F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle space=\"4\"><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> The series is convergent."
            },
